From d8874232c9007ad5de02309d9b7e06832df8cd9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yin Li <kevinli.ai.work@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 02:11:53 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] [Frontend][Core] Sampled-token logprob fast path for
 /inference/v1/generate (return_token_logprobs)

RL rollout collectors need one float per generated token: the sampled
token's logprob. On the token-in/token-out endpoint that means logprobs=0
and parsing choices[].logprobs.content[i].logprob, and on the server it
means: the scheduler slices a LogprobsLists (token ids, logprobs, ranks) per
request per step, encodes it into EngineCoreOutput, the output processor
converts it with .tolist(), detokenizes every entry and appends Logprob
objects (or FlatLogprobs), and the frontend builds a
ChatCompletionLogProbsContent Pydantic object per token before JSON. None
of that is needed for one float per token.

This adds GenerateRequest.return_token_logprobs and a matching internal
SamplingParams.sampled_logprobs_only (requires logprobs == 0):

- the scheduler emits EngineCoreOutput.new_sampled_logprobs, one float per
  new token read from column 0 of the step's logprobs array (the sampler
  stores the sampled token first), instead of a LogprobsLists;
- the output processor keeps a plain float list and the cumulative logprob,
  never builds Logprob entries and never detokenizes;
- the response carries choices[].token_logprobs: list[float] with the same
  max(x, -9999.0) clamp as the logprobs objects, and the OpenAI-style
  logprobs object is omitted. With logprobs > 0 both are returned, the
  sampled column then coming from the flat representation;
- token_logprobs is omitted from responses that did not ask for it, so the
  existing schema is unchanged;
- it requires --logprobs-mode raw_logprobs or processed_logprobs (the field
  is named for log-probabilities and does not hand back logits); streaming
  is rejected with a 400; the Rust frontend rejects the field explicitly
  rather than ignoring it, and the Rust engine-core client mirrors the new
  (last-appended) EngineCoreOutput field.

One L20 (8-core host), /inference/v1/generate, 256-token rollouts, prompts =
2 x concurrency, medians of 3 interleaved rounds, relative to the same
server with no logprobs requested. Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct: logprobs=0 objects
0.73x (c64) / 0.67x (c256); return_token_logprobs 0.96x / 0.95x. With
--return-sampling-mask the rollout contract (mask + token logprob) reaches
0.94x of that server's plain generation. Qwen3-4B: 0.95x -> 0.99x. Response
size per request ~41 KB -> ~6.8 KB; API-server CPU with logprobs returns to
the no-logprobs level. Values are identical to the object path (max abs
diff 0.0 over 16 seeded sequences under VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT=1). The GPU
kernels are not the cost: skipping _ranks_kernel is within noise and
skipping every logprob kernel is worth at most ~5 points.

Tests: flat array equals the object path's per-token logprob (greedy and
under n-gram speculative decoding with ragged multi-token steps); default
of logprobs; coexistence with logprobs > 0; n=2/4 choices; clamp of -inf
and extreme values; stream rejection; field omitted unless requested;
LogprobsLists column selection with cu_num_generated_tokens boundaries;
output-processor accumulation; SamplingParams validation; Rust round-trip.

Signed-off-by: Yin Li <kevinli.ai.work@gmail.com>
Co-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
